================================================================================
Collapsible generated-code panes in the business-rule editors
================================================================================

Context:
The visual IF/THEN editor now shows the SHACL-AF a rule compiles to. Two
follow-ups: (1) hide that generated SHACL behind a "Show SHACL code" button so
the editor stays uncluttered by default, and (2) give the Decision Table and
Aggregate rule editors the same affordance. Those two rule types have no SHACL
form — the reasoner compiles each to a SQL SELECT against the flat
(subject, predicate, object) triple table — so their pane shows the generated
Spark SQL. All three panes are read-only (transpilation / compilation is
one-directional) and collapsed by default, revealed on click.

Changes:
1. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html —
   - IF/THEN editor: wrapped the generated-SHACL preview in a collapsed
     `#swrlPreviewWrap` and added a `#swrlToggleShacl` ("Show SHACL code")
     toggle button; the advanced/read-only note stays visible outside the wrap.
   - Decision Table modal: added a "Show SQL code" toggle (`#dtToggleSql`,
     data-br-action="dt-toggle-sql") + collapsed `#dtSqlWrap` / `#dtSqlCode`
     below the "What this table does" preview.
   - Aggregate modal: same pattern (`#aggToggleSql`, "agg-toggle-sql",
     `#aggSqlWrap` / `#aggSqlCode`).
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-swrl.js —
   - Added `toggleShaclPreview()`; `_refreshShaclPreview()` now no-ops while the
     pane is collapsed (skips the fetch); `_resetEditor()` re-collapses the pane
     and resets the button on every open.
3. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js —
   - Added `dtToggleSql()` / `aggToggleSql()`, debounced
     `_dtRenderSqlPreview()` / `_aggRenderSqlPreview()` (no-op while collapsed,
     token-guarded), a shared `_fetchRuleSql()` helper, and `_resetSqlPane()`
     called from `dtOpenEditor` / `aggOpenEditor`. The existing describe-preview
     handlers also refresh the SQL when the pane is open. Wired the two new
     `data-br-action`s into the delegated dispatch.
4. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-business-rules.css —
   - Added `.br-sql-code` (dark monospaced code block, matching the IF/THEN
     SHACL pane) with scroll + wrap for long SQL.
5. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py —
   - New read-only route POST /ontology/rules/{rule_type}/preview-sql
     (decision_tables | aggregate_rules). Resolves the name-based form rule to
     URIs via the engine's own resolver, then builds the SQL with
     DecisionTableEngine.build_violation_sql / AggregateRuleEngine.build_sql
     against a placeholder "triples" table. Nothing is persisted; no store.

