================================================================================
Complex rules: fail-closed SPARQL CONSTRUCT -> SQL compiler
================================================================================

Context:
Complex (SPARQL CONSTRUCT) rules were translated by a regex-based translator
that kept only the first CONSTRUCT triple, read a single FILTER, ignored
OPTIONAL / UNION / NOT EXISTS, and returned zero triples (logged warning) when
it could not parse a query. "Validate" only checked that the text looked like a
CONSTRUCT, so a rule could save and then do nothing (or something partial) at
run time. Numeric filters also emitted Spark TRY_CAST on Lakebase Postgres,
where it is a syntax error. Complex rules now go through a compiler built on
rdflib's SPARQL algebra that accepts an explicit subset and refuses everything
else, both on save and at run time. Simple (IF/THEN, SHACL-AF) rules are
unchanged.

Scope note: the recommendation to push Complex-rule materialisation into SQL
INSERTs (like Simple rules) was not applied. The reasoning `materialize` option
means "write to an external Delta table", yet with it Simple rules also INSERT
into the graph table reference, which is the union VIEW on Delta (the INSERT
fails) and the live graph on Lakebase. Writes for Complex rules stay on the
existing append path (materialize_inferred / append_graph); that flag overload
is a follow-up.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/rules/SparqlConstructCompiler.py (new)
   Compiles a CONSTRUCT into `SELECT s, p, o` on the flat triple table (Spark /
   Postgres): connected triple patterns (disconnected patterns refused rather
   than cross-joined), FILTER with = != < > <= >=, && / ||, CONTAINS /
   STRSTARTS / STRENDS (LIKE with ESCAPE), NOT EXISTS of triple patterns, and
   any number of head triples (UNION ALL). Each head triple skips triples
   already in the store (NOT EXISTS). Undeclared prefixes resolve through the
   ontology URI map as before; declared PREFIXes keep their IRI. OPTIONAL,
   UNION, BIND, GROUP BY, LIMIT, property paths, variable predicates,
   sub-queries, EXISTS and unbound head/filter variables raise ValidationError.
2. src/back/core/reasoning/rules/SPARQLRuleEngine.py
   Delegates translation to the compiler; removed the regex translator
   (_construct_to_sql, _term_sql, _resolve_term, _translate_filter) and the
   ignored `materialize` parameter; query/compile failures now surface as
   stats `errors` / `error_details` instead of being swallowed;
   validate_rule() requires the query to compile.
3. src/back/core/reasoning/shacl_rules/RuleBuiltinRegistry.py
   New public numeric_sql(expr, dialect): TRY_CAST on Spark, regex-guarded
   ::float8 on Postgres (reuses _pg_try_cast).
4. src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py
   run_sparql_rules() drops the dead `materialize` argument; the phase copies
   errors to sparql_rules_errors / sparql_rules_error_details; module/class
   docstrings no longer list decision tables / aggregate rules.
5. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   /rules/sparql_rules/save rejects an enabled rule that does not compile (a
   disabled rule still saves, so a legacy rule can be switched off);
   /validate puts the reasons in the error message (detail is stripped in
   production).
6. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js,
   src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html
   Validate shows the server reason; the Complex pane lists the supported
   subset.
7. Stale decision-table / aggregate references removed: docstrings/comments in
   src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py (inference/start description),
   src/back/objects/simulation/Reasoning.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/quality/SqlQualityChecks.py,
   src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py,
   src/back/core/w3c/shacl/ShapeConditions.py,
   src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-conditions.js,
   src/front/static/query/js/query-dataquality.js,
   src/front/templates/ontology.html; the "Decision tables & aggregate rules"
   bullet in src/front/templates/about.html; unused AGG_FUNCTIONS /
   AGG_OPERATORS in src/back/core/reasoning/constants.py (DT_* operator maps
   kept: Data Quality conditional shapes use them).
8. docs/user-guide.md, docs/architecture.md
   New "Complex Rules (SPARQL CONSTRUCT)" section (supported subset, save
   rejection, example); architecture tree and reasoning-translation table
   updated.
9. Tests
   - tests/units/reasoning/test_sparql_construct_compiler.py (new): rules run on
     an in-memory SQLite triple table (inferred triples, dedup against known
     triples, multi-triple heads, joins, multi-triple NOT EXISTS, string
     filters with LIKE metacharacters, OR, declared prefixes), Spark/Postgres
     numeric casts, and a fail-closed battery.
   - tests/units/core/test_sql_literal_escaping.py: SPARQL-engine injection
