================================================================================
Remove SWRL naming everywhere -> IF-THEN
================================================================================

Context:
The user asked to remove every visible and internal "SWRL" reference, scope
"everything": UI text, docs, comments, code identifiers, file names, HTTP
routes, API fields and stored keys. SWRL is no longer a product surface (the
runtime is SHACL-AF and the editor authors IF/THEN rules), so the naming is
now IF-THEN throughout. Persisted data and external contracts that already
exist in saved domains, OWL files, git-sync repositories and simulations are
read in their legacy form; new writes use the new names.

Changes:
1. Rules and builtins (canonical prefix `builtin:`)
