Inference phase picker redesigned as an icon tree (Graph → Inference, Simulation → Reasoning)

Context: the two screens drew the same choice (which inference phases and which
rules run) with two different tile grids. The order was different (Graph: T-Box
first, Simulation: T-Box last), the labels and descriptions were different, and
the select-all controls were different (inline-onclick links vs btn-links). The
per-rule lists dropped under the tile in a 3+1 grid, and the JavaScript that
handles tri-state selection was written twice. Both screens now render one shared
tree. Each phase is a node with a checkbox, an icon, a description and a badge.
Simple and Complex rules expand into child rule nodes. Phases are listed in
execution order (T-Box → Simple → Graph → Complex).

Changes:
1. src/front/templates/partials/layout/_phase_tree.html (new)
   Shared Jinja partial for the phase tree. It takes tree_id, tree_ctx (counts
   and owlrl), tree_ids (phase key → checkbox id), tree_checked and
   tree_lock_tbox. It includes a toolbar (select all, unselect all, expand all,
   collapse all). No inline handlers.
2. src/front/static/global/js/phase-tree.js (new)
   `PhaseTree` class. It renders the rule nodes, handles tri-state phase
   checkboxes and cascading to child rules, expand/collapse, the n/total badges
   and a busy state. It exposes `phases()`, `ruleNames()` and `applyRules()`.
   Disabled rules get an "off" badge.
